          "kicker": "Unlikely journey",
          "heading": "Emmanuel Iyogun details his unlikely rise from teenage forward to England prop",
          "body": "Northampton prop Emmanuel Iyogun has opened up about his unconventional journey to the international stage after making his England debut off the bench against Argentina in July. Originally a teenage centre and No. 8, Iyogun was initially reluctant to transition to the front row. He struggled early on, but his relentless work ethic eventually earned him Steve Borthwick's trust. Reflecting on his development, Iyogun joked that teammate 'Alex Coles always laughs at me because he says I used to run away from rucks and just wanted to carry.'"
