          "kicker": "Eligibility twist",
          "heading": "Toulouse star Jack Willis emerges as shock option for Ireland selection",
          "body": "Toulouse back-rower Jack Willis could make a sensational international return with Ireland due to his family ancestry. The newly crowned Top 14 player of the year remains locked out of England selection because he plays his club rugby in France. However, with the RFU refusing to budge on their overseas policy, the English flanker is reportedly open to an Irish call-up. His stellar form for Toulouse makes him a highly attractive option for France's key Six Nations rivals."
